<!-- How to read the city: every kind of station has a row here (data-kind), saying its signal, formula and
     window; scripts/check.mjs fails on a station kind with no row. The org's own words (its districts, its
     landmarks' kinds, the newcomers' name) join the Height row from the config. -->
<script>
  import * as Sheet from "$lib/components/ui/sheet/index.js";
  // portal: the app's root, so the sheet takes the city's tokens and theme
  let { ui, config = {}, portal = null } = $props();
  const own = $derived([...Object.values(config.layout?.kinds ?? {}), ...(config.layout?.districts ?? []).map((d) => d.name), config.layout?.newcomers?.name].filter(Boolean).join(","));
  const patrons = $derived(config.patrons?.site ? config.patrons.site.replace(/^https?:\/\/(www\.)?/, "").replace(/\/$/, "") + (config.patrons.page ?? "").replace(/\/$/, "") : "the org's patrons page");
</script>

<Sheet.Root bind:open={ui.legend}>
<Sheet.Content side="right" portalProps={{ to: portal ?? "body" }} class="ow-legend w-[360px] gap-0 overflow-y-auto sm:max-w-[360px]">
  <Sheet.Header class="ow-card-head"><Sheet.Title class="ow-eyebrow">How to read it</Sheet.Title></Sheet.Header>
  <Sheet.Description class="ow-legend-lead">Every element is a signal, a formula and a window. Height is history; light and motion are now.</Sheet.Description>
  <dl>
    <dt data-kind="Tower,New towers,Under construction,Assembly hall,Press,Disc press,Dispatch racks,Works,Pod,{own}">Height</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> lifetime commits by people on the default branch (bots and routine accounts subtracted; a fork counts only what is ahead of upstream, a mirror none). <b>Formula</b> 16 + 14 · log₂(1 + commits / 8), one scale for every building, measured from the deck: the mark's strokes, or a plinth of the same height under a lot and under each block of the contributors' quarter. <b>Window</b> all time. Nothing shrinks; a quiet building goes dark. <b>Lights</b> the windows and the lamp are lit by a commit in the last 7 days; dark otherwise.</dd>
    <dt>One repository, one parcel</dt><dd>Every repository has one building, and everything about it stands on its parcel: the building, and on the dock in front its pallet, its capsules, its workers and its name. The kind of building follows the district: a workshop with a sawtooth roof (apps), a cabinet tower (themes and plugins), a lattice mast (sites), a silo (upstream), a hand-built landmark, or one of four towers on a lot. A parcel is kept for good; an unclaimed one is an outline on the deck.</dd>
    <dt>Lamps</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commits. <b>Formula</b> a pulsing lamp at one or more. <b>Window</b> the last 7 days. The arcology's crown, antennas and a site mast's ring follow the same rule.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Themes and plugins">Drawers</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commits. <b>Formula</b> 1 + 1.5 · log₂(1 + commits) drawers stand out of a cabinet tower, in an order fixed per repository. <b>Window</b> the last 7 days.</dd>
    <dt>Plaques</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> releases. <b>Formula</b> 1.5 · log₂(1 + releases) plates on a post at the dock's corner. <b>Window</b> all time.</dd>
    <dt>Pallets</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> open pull requests. <b>Formula</b> 2 · log₂(1 + open) crates, four to a layer, the exact count stencilled with the name. <b>Window</b> now.</dd>
    <dt>Capsules</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> distinct commits that exist only on branches. <b>Formula</b> 1.4 · log₂(1 + commits) capsules plugged on a spine beside the pallet: work bolted on, not yet built in. <b>Window</b> the last 30 days.</dd>
    <dt>Workers</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> people who committed to the repository. <b>Formula</b> one each, as many as the dock holds (eight at most). <b>Window</b> the last 7 days. The people card lists everyone who committed in the 30-day window, the org members (marked org), most active first.</dd>
    <dt>Belts</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commits on the stations that feed the belt; commits by bots and routine accounts counted apart. <b>Formula</b> one crate per commit by people, one low dark tote per bot or routine commit, placed at the time it landed (data without commit times spreads a day's commits over the day); when a belt cannot hold them all, every k-th is shown; faster where the week was busier, bots included. Bots move belts but never build: no height, no lamp, no worker. <b>Window</b> the last 7 days. The themes and plugins, sites and upstream ship by drone.</dd>
    <dt>Drones</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commits per station. <b>Formula</b> one drone for each of the 14 busiest stations, flying to the landing pad on the arcology, more often where the week was busier. <b>Window</b> the last 7 days.</dd>
    <dt>Day columns</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commits across the org. <b>Formula</b> one column per calendar day (UTC), one crate per 25 commits, up to 24. An empty plate is a day with nothing landed. <b>Window</b> 30 days.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Archive">Archive</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> an archived repository's lifetime commits. <b>Formula</b> the one height scale, drawn as an outline only, so a ghost keeps its history and hides nothing behind it. <b>Window</b> all time.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Contributor">Contributors' quarter</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> a person's lifetime commits to the public repositories (bots excluded). <b>Formula</b> one building per person on the one height scale: a low-rise for a first few commits (six kinds), a tower beyond (seven kinds), the kind fixed by the login; the windows and the lamp lit by a commit. <b>Window</b> all time; the lights the last 7 days. Never removed; in rings around the mark, the ring next to the mark first, nearest the arcology, each block on a plinth as tall as the deck. A first contribution builds a new house, in scaffolding under a crane for its first day.</dd>
    <dt>Blocks and streets</dt><dd>The quarter is cut into blocks by avenues every third cell and a ring road around the mark, with amber street lamps. A block's nine plots hold its houses; a block the quarter has not reached yet holds low scenery. About one cell in nine is civic: a stadium, a monument, a park, a plaza or a transit station. Streets, lamps and civic cells are scenery; no house or repository ever takes a civic cell.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Patron board">Patron boards</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> the corporate tiers of {patrons}, read from {config.patrons?.repo ? `the ${config.patrons.repo} repository` : "the org's patrons file"}. <b>Formula</b> the {config.patrons?.crown?.label ?? "crown tier"}s on the four faces of the arcology's crown; the {config.patrons?.boards?.label ?? "board tier"}s on the billboard towers, three screens each, then on gantries across the ring road along the mark's front edge; each screen opens its patron's card, and a new patron on the page plays patron.new (an amber drop and ring on its board). Boards follow the page; each is a lit screen in a bezel, its name and mark in white, the wide screen's second line crawling the tier, the name and the link, its light spilling on the shaft; a band under each tower's cap crawls the latest commits. <b>Window</b> now.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Basecamp ward">Basecamp wards</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> the org's Basecamp projects, members only. <b>Formula</b> one ward per project on a civic cell near the repositories it steers: the hall's windows lit by this week's events, the mast's lamp by a message this week, a lantern on the hill per tracked list at its hill position, a car in the rail yard per card and a track per column, a scaffold per to-do list under way, and the archive. The public city shows the hall and mast dark and unlabelled. Height carries no count. <b>Window</b> now; events, the last 7 days.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Water tower">Water tower</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> the relay's own health, not the org's. <b>Formula</b> the water is the snapshot's freshness, full while the last scan is within one scan interval (an hour by default) and empty two intervals later, in eighths; the lamp is the live stream, steady while connected, pulsing while it reconnects, dark without a relay. <b>Window</b> now.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Capsule tower">Capsule tower</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> a repository's lifetime commits, and whether it had a commit in the last 7 days. <b>Formula</b> the city's one height scale; capsules bolted to two cores up to that height, their windows lit by this week's commits. <b>Window</b> lifetime; lights, the last 7 days. A plugin kit (city/plugins/kits/capsule.js), taken by a repository in city.config.json.</dd>
    <dt data-kind="Stars">Stars</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> a GitHub star on a repository. <b>Formula</b> one small violet ring at its roof. <b>Window</b> live. A plugin effect (city/plugins/effects/star.js).</dd>
    <dt>Colour</dt><dd>Cyan is what you selected or hover; magenta is live (a pulsing lamp, a tail light). Four quiet signage hues (blue, magenta, amber, violet) belong to patron screens, the crown, monuments and street light, and carry no count.</dd>
    <dt>Ticker</dt><dd><b>Signal</b> commit subjects. <b>Formula</b> the 24 latest crawl across the warehouse board in accent colour, with the window's total. <b>Window</b> 30 days.</dd>
    <dt>Live</dt><dd>When the page is connected to the relay, every event plays once on the building it concerns, within seconds: a drone with one crate per commit flies from a push to the arcology and the authors' house lamps ring; a crate drops onto a roof for a new pull request or branch; a beam runs to the crown for a merge; magenta smoke rises from a failed build; a launch leaves the arcology's pad for a release and every lamp blinks; rings mark the rest. Effects leave nothing behind; the building the event changed is redrawn in place with its new numbers.</dd>
    <dt>New towers</dt><dd>A repository without a district, or whose district is full, claims the next free lot and keeps its district's kind of building there; with the live stream it appears the moment it is created. A lot that holds a scenery high-rise goes only to a repository at least as tall, so a claim never lowers the skyline; when the mark is full, the rings around it open, between the contributors' blocks. For its first two weeks a new building stands in scaffolding under a crane, rising as the days pass. A repository that leaves the data leaves a vacant parcel.</dd>
    <dt>Scenery</dt><dd>Towers, cooling towers, the duct, the truck, forklifts, tanks, sheds, sky bridges, searchlights, sky cars, streets, lamps, the courtyard's boulevard, the arcology's crown deck and mast array, stadiums, monuments, parks, plazas and transit stations carry no data, have no name on the ground, and never stand taller than 60 (a building with about 70 commits).</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>The city stands on the Omarchy mark. Drag to orbit, right-drag or drag with two fingers to pan, scroll or pinch to zoom; the arrows (Q / E) turn the city 45°. Click a station to open it. The city redraws itself as new activity comes in.</p>
</Sheet.Content>
</Sheet.Root>
